<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chucuito</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chucuito is a town on the western shore of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-titicaca">Lake Titicaca</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puno">Puno</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>. Before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a> conquest it was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aymara">Aymara</a> Lupaca kingdom, and under Spanish rule it was the centre of a large royal province. A detailed Spanish inspection of 1567 by Garci <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diez">Diez</a> de San Miguel is a key source on Lupaca society.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chucuito.jpg" alt="Chucuito" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. Alfredobi assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Localizaci%C3%B3n_de_Chucuito.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
